            <ArticleTitle>Homologous physiological effects of nutritional antioxidants and eicosapentaenoic acid.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-103</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dietary fish oils rich in eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA) possess immunostimulant, anti-inflammatory, cancer-retardant, antithrombotic and ischemia-protective properties that are remarkably parallel to the effects of high-dose nutritional antioxidants. EPA and nutritional antioxidants may show complementary activities in a wide range of preventive and therapeutic applications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
